        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=(-1,-7)$",
          "worked": "Subtract the first equation from the second.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x&=-3\\\\x&=-1\\\\2(-1)-y&=5\\\\-y&=7\\\\y&=-7\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $(x,y)=(-1,-7)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q15-i",
