        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y)=\\left(-\\frac{11}{2},\\frac12\\right)$",
          "worked": "Subtract the second equation from the first.\n$$\\begin{align*}10y&=5\\\\y&=\\frac12\\\\-x+3\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=7\\\\-x+\\frac32&=7\\\\-x&=\\frac{11}{2}\\\\x&=-\\frac{11}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $(x,y)=\\left(-\\frac{11}{2},\\frac12\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      },
      {
